  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredOnAllOps  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequiredOnAllOps.als
    rationale: Removing the auth-required fact lets Alloy invent an Operation with no caller but outcome Accepted, which is exactly what FR-001 and the AuthRequiredEverywhere pattern forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Removing the append-only constraint on task_deletions lets two TaskDeletion rows reference the same Task, violating the permanence/append-only guarantee.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_DeletionPermanent
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_DeletionPermanent: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeleteAcceptedProducesDeletion  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeleteAcceptedProducesDeletion.als
    rationale: Removing the produces-deletion fact lets an accepted DELETE happen without writing a task_deletions row, which is the exact audit-completeness failure mode for FR-018.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionAttribution  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing the deletion-attribution fact lets the deletion row record a deleter that is not the calling user, which the AttributionCorrectness pattern explicitly forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_018_DeletionLogged
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLogged: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: Removing the closed-task-edit rule lets Alloy accept a PATCH on a done task that does not simultaneously reopen it, which FR-011 (and US2 #5/#6) forbid.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ValidationBeforeMutation  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ValidationBeforeMutation.als
    rationale: Removing the validation-before-mutation fact lets a rejected CreateOp still produce a Task row, which violates the atomicity contract in data-model.md and the validation gate for FR-005..FR-008.
    expected to FAIL: ValidationBeforeMutation, FR_002_IdentityFromAuth
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_IdentityFromAuth: PASS (vacuous?)

